---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';

/* Written from what the code actually does. Bundle sets no cookies: grep the
   repository for document.cookie and you get nothing. Everything it remembers
   is localStorage, listed item by item below, and the only third-party request
   any page makes is the Google Fonts stylesheet. Say that plainly rather than
   publishing the usual four-category boilerplate that describes no real site. */

const stored = [
  { key: 'bundle.consent', what: 'Your answer to the cookie banner, and when you gave it.', why: 'Essential', life: 'Until you clear it or change your mind.' },
  { key: 'bundle.display', what: 'Text size, contrast, motion and link preferences.', why: 'Essential', life: 'Until reset.' },
  { key: 'bundle.user', what: 'The email and display name on your local account.', why: 'Essential', life: 'Until you sign out or delete your data.' },
  { key: 'bundle.profile', what: 'Your saved investor profile: ticket size, target spread, sectors.', why: 'Essential', life: 'Until you delete it.' },
  { key: 'bundle.profileDraft', what: 'A part-finished questionnaire, so a refresh does not lose your answers.', why: 'Essential', life: 'Until you finish or delete it.' },
  { key: 'bundle.holdings', what: 'Positions you told us you took after visiting a venue.', why: 'Essential', life: 'Until you delete them.' },
  { key: 'bundle.lessons', what: 'Which Academy lessons you have completed.', why: 'Essential', life: 'Until reset.' },
  { key: 'bundle.watchlist', what: 'Companies you starred on the screener.', why: 'Essential', life: 'Until you unstar them.' },
  { key: 'bundle.pendingTrade', what: 'That you opened a venue, so we can ask whether you went through with it.', why: 'Essential', life: 'Cleared once you answer.' },
  { key: 'bundle.navHintSeen', what: 'That you have already seen the one-off pointer to your dashboard.', why: 'Essential', life: 'Permanent, so we only show it once.' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie policy"
  description="Bundle sets no cookies. This page lists every item it stores in your browser, what each one is for, how long it lasts and how to remove it."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Cookie policy"
    lead="Last updated: 29 September 2026 · Bundle sets no cookies at all. Here is every single thing it does store, and how to clear it."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <div class="callout">
          <p><strong>The short version</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Bundle sets <strong>no cookies</strong>, first-party or third-party.</li>
            <li>What it remembers lives in your browser's local storage and is never transmitted to us.</li>
            <li>There are no advertising tags, no analytics scripts, no pixels and no fingerprinting on this site today.</li>
            <li>
              One third party is contacted: Google Fonts, for the typefaces.
              <a href="#third-parties">What that means</a>.
            </li>
            <li>
              You can change your answer at any time:
              <button type="button" class="text-link" data-cookie-prefs>
                open cookie preferences <span class="arrow">→</span>
              </button>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h2>Why there is a banner at all</h2>
        <p>
          Under the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations, consent
          is needed before non-essential information is stored on or read from
          your device. Bundle stores nothing non-essential today, so strictly
          it could show you no banner. It shows one anyway for a simple reason:
          the decision is recorded <em>before</em> anything optional exists, and
          the code checks that decision before any optional feature can run.
          That is the opposite of the usual order, where the tags fire first and
          the banner apologises afterwards.
        </p>
        <p>
          "Essential only" and "Accept all" are the same size and the same
          colour, both optional categories start switched off, and closing the
          banner without choosing is not treated as agreement.
        </p>

        <h2>What Bundle stores on your device</h2>
        <p>
          All of the following are <strong>local storage</strong> entries, not
          cookies. The practical difference matters: cookies are attached to
          every request your browser makes to a server, whereas these are never
          sent anywhere. This site is a static build with no application server
          behind it, so there is nowhere for them to go.
        </p>

        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Name</th>
                <th>What it holds</th>
                <th>Category</th>
                <th>How long</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {
                stored.map((s) => (
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">{s.key}</code></td>
                    <td>{s.what}</td>
                    <td>{s.why}</td>
                    <td>{s.life}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h2>Optional categories</h2>
        <p>
          Two categories appear in the banner and are switched off unless you
          turn them on. Nothing currently uses either one; they exist so that
          the day something does, your answer is already on record and is
          honoured from the first page load rather than retro-fitted.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Analytics.</strong> Aggregate counts of which pages get
            read, measured without cross-site tracking, advertising identifiers
            or fingerprinting.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Personalisation.</strong> Remembering your screener filters
            and recently viewed companies between visits.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="third-parties">Third parties</h2>
        <p>
          Every page loads its typefaces from Google Fonts
          (<code class="mono">fonts.googleapis.com</code> and
          <code class="mono">fonts.gstatic.com</code>). Google does not set
          cookies for font requests, but your IP address and browser details
          reach Google in order to serve the files, and that is a transfer we
          should name rather than leave out. No other third-party domain is
          contacted by this site: no tag managers, no ad networks, no embedded
          video, no chat vendors. The assistant in the corner runs entirely in
          your browser from data this site already ships.
        </p>

        <h2>How to clear everything</h2>
        <p>
          Two routes, both immediate. Use
          <a href="/legal/data-deletion">delete my data</a> on this site, which
          removes every entry in the table above in one click. Or clear site
          data for bundle.ai in your browser's settings, which does the same
          thing from the browser's side. There is no server copy to chase,
          because there is no server copy.
        </p>
        <p>
          Blocking local storage entirely will leave the site readable. The
          screener, the company pages and the Academy all work; what stops
          working is anything that has to remember you, so your plan, your
          holdings and your progress will not persist between pages.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If Bundle ever adds a cookie or a genuine analytics tool, this page
          gets the entry, the banner gets the category, and the "last updated"
          date changes. We will not quietly widen an existing category to cover
          something new.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions: <a href="mailto:privacy@bundle.ai">privacy@bundle.ai</a>.
          See also the <a href="/legal/privacy">privacy policy</a> and
          <a href="/legal/data-deletion">data deletion policy</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .callout > p { margin: 0; }
  .callout ul { margin: 0.5rem 0 0; }

  .prose code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }

  /* The preferences control is a button because it opens a dialog rather
     than navigating; it should still read as the link it looks like. */
  .prose button.text-link {
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    padding: 0;
    font: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
</style>
